The body AB Connect returns for a request carrying a bad signature.

VERBATIM from a live probe, gate G-5 result in 01-sdk-v3.md section 12, run 2026-08-02 against devel
partner sws:

  a bad-signature request returned
  401 {"errors":[{"status":"401","title":"Unauthorized","detail":"Signature is not authorized."}]}

The file is that body, byte for byte, with nothing added and nothing reformatted. It is deliberately
kept on one line the way the service sent it, because a test that pretty-prints a fixture is no longer
testing the wire.

Documented shape:
  https://developerdocs.instructure.com/services/ab-connect/introduction/error-responses.md
  which specifies JSON:API errors[] with source.pointer, source.parameter, detail, status, and title.
  01-sdk-v3.md section 5.2 maps this shape onto ABConnectApiError.

What a test must assert from it:
  - ABConnectResponseMapper.ParseErrors returns exactly one ABConnectApiError.
  - Status is the STRING "401", not the number 401. AB Connect sends it quoted, per JSON:API, and
    ABConnectApiError.Status is string? for that reason.
  - Title is "Unauthorized" and Detail is "Signature is not authorized.".
  - SourcePointer and SourceParameter are both null: this body carries no "source" member at all, and
    an absent member must read as null rather than as an empty string.
  - A 401 response carrying this body maps to ABConnectAuthenticationException, whose Errors property
    carries the parsed list.

Why the Errors list matters here specifically, and not just as a nicety: section 5.2 records that AB
Connect documents 401 as meaning bad credentials OR an unlicensed call ("It may be that your current
license does not support the call you are making"). The two are only distinguishable by reading
detail, so an exception that dropped the parsed errors would make them indistinguishable to the
caller. That is why ABConnectRequestException.Errors exists and why it is never null.

A fixture must never contain a partner id, a partner key, or a signature. This one does not: the
service echoes no query back in an error body.
